IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch5`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch5a`

-- Tests for ssc9-sch5a.l4 (Schedule 5A). Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- Schedule 5A`

`sch 5A test twelve months exactly` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025
`sch 5A test a day short of twelve months` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 30 12 2025
`sch 5A test leap day start, 27 February` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 29 2 2024, `the last day` IS Date 27 2 2025
`sch 5A test the first quarter of 2025` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 3 2025

§§ `Paragraph 1`

-- Expected: deferred and 12 months -> must elect (true); under 12 months, not deferred, or the leap-day fork day -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 1(1) the person must elect` TRUE `sch 5A test twelve months exactly` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 1(1) the person must elect` TRUE `sch 5A test a day short of twelve months` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 1(1) the person must elect` FALSE `sch 5A test twelve months exactly` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 1(1) the person must elect` TRUE `sch 5A test leap day start, 27 February` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The duty, prescribed period 14 days. Read by eye: an election on day 3 -> FULFILLED; a lapse to day 15 -> FULFILLED (1(2) deems the lump sum).
#TRACE `sch 5A para 1(1) the election duty` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 5A the person whose entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred` DOES `sch 5A makes an election` `sch 5A para 1(1)(a) an election that paragraph 2 (the increase of pension) applies` AT 3
#TRACE `sch 5A para 1(1) the election duty` 14 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 1(2) the election that is treated as made` NOTHING EQUALS `sch 5A para 1(1)(b) an election that paragraph 4 (the lump sum) applies`
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 1(2) the election that is treated as made` (JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(a) an election that paragraph 2 (the increase of pension) applies`) EQUALS `sch 5A para 1(1)(a) an election that paragraph 2 (the increase of pension) applies`

§§ `Paragraph 2`

-- Expected: under 12 months -> applies; 12 months with the increase election -> applies; 12 months with the lump-sum election or no election -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 2(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE `sch 5A test a day short of twelve months` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 2(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE `sch 5A test twelve months exactly` (JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(a) an election that paragraph 2 (the increase of pension) applies`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 2(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE `sch 5A test twelve months exactly` (JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(b) an election that paragraph 4 (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 2(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE `sch 5A test twelve months exactly` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 2(1) this paragraph applies` FALSE `sch 5A test a day short of twelve months` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 2(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE `sch 5A test leap day start, 27 February` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2(2): rate 50: 0.50 is exactly 1 per cent (increase 0.5); 0.49 is not enough (0).
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 2(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` 0.5 50 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 2(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` 0.49 50 EQUALS 0

§§ `Paragraph 3`

-- 3(5) and 3(1): six days of increment per period: 13 -> 2, 5 -> 0.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3(5) the number of complete incremental periods` 13 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3(5) the number of complete incremental periods` 5 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3(1) the number of increments` 7 EQUALS 7
-- 3(3), (4): 0.004 -> 0; 0.005 -> 0.01; 1.234 -> 1.23; 1.235 -> 1.24.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3(3) the amount under sub-paragraph (2) as rounded` 0.004 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3(3) the amount under sub-paragraph (2) as rounded` 0.005 EQUALS 0.01
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3(3) the amount under sub-paragraph (2) as rounded` 1.234 EQUALS 1.23
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3(3) the amount under sub-paragraph (2) as rounded` 1.235 EQUALS 1.24
-- 3(2): rate 100 -> 0.2; rate 122.5 -> 0.245 -> 0.25.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3(2) the increment for one incremental period` 100 EQUALS 0.2
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3(2) the increment for one incremental period` 122.5 EQUALS 0.25
-- The aggregate: rate 122.5, 12 days = 2 x 0.25 = 0.5.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3 the aggregate of the increments` 122.5 12 EQUALS 0.5
-- 3(6).
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3(6) the rate for an incremental period` TRUE 110 EQUALS JUST 110
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 3(6) the rate for an incremental period` FALSE 110 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph 2 as a whole: under 12 months, rate 200, 30 days = 5 x 0.4 = 2.0 = exactly 1 per cent -> 2; 29 days = 4 x 0.4 = 1.6 -> 0; lump sum election -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 2 the amount by which the shared additional pension is increased for the deferment` TRUE `sch 5A test a day short of twelve months` NOTHING 200 30 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 2 the amount by which the shared additional pension is increased for the deferment` TRUE `sch 5A test a day short of twelve months` NOTHING 200 29 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 2 the amount by which the shared additional pension is increased for the deferment` TRUE `sch 5A test twelve months exactly` (JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(b) an election that paragraph 4 (the lump sum) applies`) 200 30 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 4`

#ASSERT `sch 5A para 4(2) the person is entitled to a lump sum` TRUE (JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(b) an election that paragraph 4 (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 4(2) the person is entitled to a lump sum` TRUE (JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(a) an election that paragraph 2 (the increase of pension) applies`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 4(2) the person is entitled to a lump sum` FALSE (JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(b) an election that paragraph 4 (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 5`

-- Prescribed day Monday (1); 6 Jan 2025 is the first Monday of 2025; the deferment 1 Jan to 31 Mar 2025 ends on a Monday.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(2) an accrual period begins on the day` (Date 6 1 2025) 1 `sch 5A test the first quarter of 2025`
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 5A para 5(2) an accrual period begins on the day` (Date 7 1 2025) 1 `sch 5A test the first quarter of 2025`)
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(1) the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment` 1 `sch 5A test the first quarter of 2025` EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 31 3 2025, `the last day` IS Date 6 4 2025)
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(1) the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment` 1 (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 3 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 5(3): the formula is omitted from the text -> NOTHING; R is base rate plus 2, or a higher prescribed rate.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(3) the accrued amount for an accrual period` 0 80 6 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(3) the percentage rate R` 4 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(3) the percentage rate R` 4 (JUST 8) EQUALS JUST 8
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(3) the percentage rate R` 4 (JUST 6) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 5(4): a change on Wednesday 8 Jan 2025 takes effect Monday 13 Jan 2025.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(4) the day a change in the base rate is treated as taking effect` (Date 8 1 2025) 1 NOTHING EQUALS Date 13 1 2025
-- 5(5): 80 less a prescribed 5 = 75; nothing prescribed -> 80.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(5) the amount of shared additional pension counted for an accrual period` 80 5 EQUALS 75
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(5) the amount of shared additional pension counted for an accrual period` 80 0 EQUALS 80
-- 5(6): 7.345 -> 7.35; 7.3449 -> 7.34.
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(6) the lump sum as rounded` 7.345 EQUALS 7.35
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(6) the lump sum as rounded` 7.3449 EQUALS 7.34
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(1) the lump sum before rounding` (JUST 7.345) EQUALS JUST 7.345
#ASSERT `sch 5A para 5(1) the lump sum before rounding` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
